1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,234
The trial run began with a limited prospect and a heated argument about the heat itself: could a beautiful old building be made cool without being ruined?

2
00:00:09,234 --> 00:00:15,183
“I suggest we test two rooms and let the results occur,” Lin said.

3
00:00:15,183 --> 00:00:25,706
“We intend to do a real evaluation, not a prediction.” The feeling in the room was that the issue would embarrass them both.

4
00:00:25,706 --> 00:00:31,309
The passion of the meeting was genuine and the accuracy of the numbers was not.

5
00:00:31,309 --> 00:00:37,873
“We have too much expectation and too little sensitivity,” the engineer said.

6
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:51,690
“A wealthy client will opt for the outward look; a poor tenant will perceive the inward cost.” The five of them had, probably, two months and one chance.

7
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:57,024
The possibility of a postponement arrived with the first cold night.

8
00:00:57,024 --> 00:01:04,352
“Yesterday the plan was obvious, and tomorrow it will be scandalous,” the director said.

9
00:01:04,352 --> 00:01:12,000
“We underestimated the vigor of the winter, and we let the hope of a quick fix madden us.”

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,094
The disgust that followed was not intentional; it came from a bad measurement.

11
00:01:18,094 --> 00:01:23,223
“You can explode with passion and still be wrong,” Maya wrote.

12
00:01:23,223 --> 00:01:38,879
“Happiness is not a design criterion, and goodness is not a discount.” The inward and the outward temperature had been recorded twenty times, and the history of the building had been read only once.

13
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:44,893
“How do we waken the council without overwhelming it?” the engineer asked.

14
00:01:44,893 --> 00:02:02,249
“Damn the schedule; a two-week delay is better than a scandal.” The sensitivity of the sensor, the accuracy of the survey, and the real cost of the work were all, yet again, in the same unhappy column.

15
00:02:02,249 --> 00:02:13,911
The trial run ended with a small, useful result and one new constraint: the group would have to be awake to the difference between what they deem true and what they can prove.

16
00:02:13,911 --> 00:02:19,480
The choice that had a cost was the choice to publish the weak number first.

17
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:30,812
Although we believe in the plan, the order of the moment is to try a smaller version, because a passionate and dramatically wrong forecast is not foresight.

18
00:02:30,812 --> 00:02:39,577
A promise can bind two people without binding the outcome, and a kind fall is still a fall.
